The first iPhone Duo teardown videos have been shared by YouTube channels <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3MSg-ZOfqGA">REWA Technology</a> and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=luPfYDpDIfQ">Phone Repair Guru</a>, providing us with a look inside the device.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iPhone-Duo-Outer-Display-Hand-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072686" /><br/>
iPhone Duo has two battery cells that can be removed with electrically-activated adhesive. There is a larger battery with a 2,962 mAh (11.56 Wh) capacity and a smaller one that is rated at 1,921 mAh (7.5 Wh). Total battery capacity <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/18/iphone-duo-battery-capacity/">is 4,883 mAh</a>.<br/>
<br/>
REWA Technology's video includes a labeled breakdown of the logic board, which contains Apple's A20 Pro chip, C2 cellular modem, and more.<br/>
<br/>
